{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "radiation-biology",
    "title": "Radiation Biology",
    "order": 7
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "cell-structure",
    "title": "Cell Structure",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "The Cell as a Radiobiology Starting Point",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Every effect covered elsewhere in this module \u2014 survival curves, cell sensitivity, DNA damage, the four R's \u2014 ultimately traces back to how a single cell is built and how it operates. This lesson is the basic map."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Composition of a Cell",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A cell consists of a "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "cell (plasma) membrane",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " enclosing "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "cytoplasm",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", within which sit various "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "organelles",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", and a "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "nucleus",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " containing the cell's genetic material."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The cell membrane's phospholipid bilayer controls what passes into and out of the cell \u2014 and as covered in the DNA Damage lesson, this membrane is itself a real (if secondary) target for radiation damage."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Key Organelles",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Organelle"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Function"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Mitochondria"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Energy production (cellular respiration)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Ribosomes"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Protein synthesis"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Endoplasmic reticulum"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Transport network; processes proteins and lipids"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Golgi apparatus"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Packages and ships proteins for use inside or outside the cell"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Lysosomes"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Break down waste and cellular debris"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Radiation damage to mitochondrial or lysosomal membranes specifically can have severe downstream consequences for the whole cell \u2014 energy production and waste processing are both disrupted."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The Nucleus and DNA",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "nucleus",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " houses the cell's DNA, organized into chromosomes. DNA carries the instructions for building proteins and directing every cellular function \u2014 and as covered in the DNA Damage lesson, it's considered the single most critical target for radiation-induced cell death."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page4_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Which organelle is responsible for energy production within the cell?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Mitochondria",
              "Ribosomes"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Mitochondria carry out cellular respiration, producing the cell's usable energy."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The Cell Cycle",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Cells progress through a repeating cycle: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "G1",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (growth, preparing for DNA synthesis) \u2192 "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "S",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (DNA synthesis/replication) \u2192 "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "G2",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (further growth, preparing for division) \u2192 "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "M",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (mitosis \u2014 the cell divides into two identical daughter cells)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "As covered in Cell Survival Curves, radiosensitivity varies dramatically depending on which phase a cell is in when irradiated \u2014 most sensitive in G2/M, most resistant in late S."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered basic cell composition, key organelles and their functions, the nucleus/DNA relationship, and the cell cycle phases."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "This foundational map is what makes the rest of the Radiation Biology module make sense \u2014 every other lesson here builds on these basic structures and processes."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
